=== K1: dimensional closure (sympy, exact) ===
  exponent matrix (rows L, M, T; cols G, c, rho, M) =
    [[3, 1, -3, 0], [-1, 0, 1, 1], [-2, -1, 0, 0]]
  rank = 3 of 4 unknowns  -> solution space dimension = 1
  particular solution (g = 0)  (a, b, g, m) = [-1, 4, 0, -1]   [= c^4 / (G M)]
  nullspace direction (normalised on rho) = [3, -6, 1, 2]   [= G^3 rho M^2 / c^6 = (G M sqrt(G rho)/c^3)^2, dimensionless]
  general monomial exponents  (a, b, g, m) = [3*t - 1, 4 - 6*t, t, 2*t - 1]
  mass-independence (m = 2t - 1 = 0) requires t = 1/2; then (a, b, g, m) = [1/2, 1, 1/2, 0]  -> c^1 G^(1/2) rho^(1/2) M^0 = c sqrt(G rho)
  rank==3: True | nullspace == (3,-6,1,2): True | t=1/2 -> (1/2,1,1/2,0): True
  m(t) = 0 has the single root t = 1/2 : True
  K1 PASS: True
  ---> Q1 (form): universality (no M in a_0) forces a_0 = Phi * c sqrt(G rho_*) UNIQUELY.
       Which rho_* is, and Phi (=kappa) is, are separate questions. K1 does not touch either.

